The proposed solution has an error: it states pq < 25, but actually pq < √1000 ≈ 31.6. This means the pair (2, 13) with pq = 26 also qualifies: 26² = 676 < 1000, which gives another number with nine divisors. Checking further pairs: (2,17) gives 34² = 1156 > 1000, and (3,11) gives 33² = 1089 > 1000, so no others.

Correct sum: 36 + 100 + 196 + 225 + 441 + 484 + 676 + 256 = 2414.

